    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0790" n="1624" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/254</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-24T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4175. For McFadden [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 92. Please note the following and repeat to Dresel.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Your No. 34, Legation 3361, May 14, 5 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d667-f1"/> We
                        agree to your suggestion that raw materials destined for use in Switzerland
                        in the manufacture of munitions for the Allies be not consigned to the
                        S[ociété] S[uisse de] S[urveillance Economique] or reckoned in the Swiss
                        ration. We will rely upon you to insure that such exports are <pb
                            facs="0791" n="1625" xml:id="pg1625"/> properly safeguarded and will
                        actually be employed in the manufacture of munitions; we understand that you
                        will cable us of what shipments should be licensed in accordance with this
                        special procedure. We feel it important that there should be very close
                        coordination in Switzerland of the representatives of the Associated
                        Governments who are supervising the production of munitions.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
